## F1 — Card Close Behaviour

The CTA button at the bottom of each milestone card is the **primary and intended** method for dismissing the card. The X button in the top right corner may remain as a secondary escape hatch, but the designed flow should always guide the user toward the CTA button.

### Behaviour Rules

- The card **never auto-closes** under any circumstance.
- The user must always manually confirm by clicking the CTA button at the bottom.
- Each milestone already has unique CTA text defined in `data/milestones.ts` — use these as the button labels (e.g. `"BROADCAST DATA"`, `"SYNC CREW LOGS"`, `"VALIDATE VITALS"`).
- The X button in the top right can remain but should be visually de-emphasized relative to the CTA button.

