## F3 — Role Onboarding: "Systems Online" Sequence

After the user selects their role on the Role Selection screen, instead of the trajectory appearing immediately, the interface **builds itself in staggered layers** — like a cockpit powering up. This sequence ends with a role-specific intro transmission card that onboards the user before they begin.

### Stagger Sequence — In Order

1. Background sharpens or fades into full visibility.
2. HUD corner elements flicker on — `MISSION STATUS / TELEM_ACTIVE` top left, `COORD_SYSTEM / UTM_WGS84_V2.2` top right.
3. Earth globe appears in the bottom left.
4. Moon appears in the top right.
5. The trajectory SVG path **draws itself** as a line from Earth toward the Moon — like a flight path being plotted on a radar screen.
6. Milestone nodes **blink on one by one** along the path in sequence.
7. The intro transmission card **animates in** — slides up from below or fades in at center screen.

**Total sequence duration:** approximately 3–4 seconds. Each layer should have a staggered delay of roughly 300–500ms after the previous. Expose all stagger timings as named constants.

### The Intro Transmission Card

This card uses the **exact same component and visual design** as the existing milestone transmission cards. No new design is needed. Content is role-dependent — read the `role` value from the Zustand store.

#### Mission Control Copy

> In 2025, we mastered the orbit, providing the strategy and certainty of execution that our clients rely on to fund more than three loans every single business day. Your mission today is to serve as the signal through the noise, guiding our brave commanders across the lunar landscape to a successful landing.
>
> Initiate Launch Sequence by clicking the launch milestone.

#### Commander Copy

> 2025 was a year of extraordinary transit, where your vision shaped the cityscapes we see today. In a market of shifting gravity and atmospheric pressure, you stayed the course. Your objective today is to reach the moon and secure your project's future with the unwavering guidance of Mission Control.
>
> Initiate Launch Sequence by clicking the launch milestone.

### CTA Button

Single button at the bottom of the intro card. Label: **`"INITIATE SEQUENCE"`**. Clicking it dismisses the card and leaves the user on the fully revealed trajectory, ready to interact with the Launch milestone node.

### Session Persistence

This intro card is a **one-time onboarding moment per session**. Once dismissed, it must not reappear if the user navigates back or refreshes mid-session. Add a boolean flag to the Zustand store:

```ts
hasSeenIntro: false  // set to true when INITIATE SEQUENCE is clicked
```

