## S3 — Commander Role: Color Palette Refinement

The current Commander experience uses saturated `ici-red` (#D80010) as the dominant color across all UI elements. This reads as **alarm and urgency** rather than prestige and leadership. The palette should shift so that **white and off-white become the primary UI color**, with red reserved exclusively for deliberate moments of emphasis.

The contrast makes red accents hit harder — when everything is white and one button is red, that button commands the room.

### Commander Color Roles — Before & After

| UI Element | Current | New |
|---|---|---|
| Trajectory path | `ici-red` | White / off-white |
| Node indicators | `ici-red` glow | White / white glow |
| Card borders & glass highlights | `ici-red` | White / off-white |
| Comet travelling light | `ici-red` | White / off-white |
| HUD text & labels | Light (unchanged) | No change |
| CTA button | `ici-red` | `ici-red` ✅ keep |
| Active node indicator | `ici-red` | `ici-red` ✅ keep |
| Pulsing logo glow in card header | `ici-red` | `ici-red` ✅ keep |

### Role Selection Screen

The Commander card on the Role Selection screen must also reflect this refined palette. The current red-dominant card treatment should shift toward **white/off-white with subtle red accents only**.

The visual contrast between the two role cards becomes **"White & Blue"** rather than "Red & Blue":
- **Mission Control** — retains full `amg-blue` identity
- **Commander** — takes on a clean, authoritative white character with red used only as punctuation

### Mission Control — No Changes

The `amg-blue` (#009DD6) palette for Mission Control remains **completely unchanged** throughout the entire experience.

